  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IPPC_2</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">IPPC_2</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Based on a request from the Ministry of Environmental Protection in Serbia the second phase of a project reducing industrial emissions and strengthening Serbia&#xb4;s EU accession process with a focus on Integrated Pollution Prevention and Control (IPPC) and the Industrial Emissions Direcive (IED). The project gives special attention to the food sector performance. Activities will aim at supporting the preparation of the negotiation position of Chapter 27, the EU environmental policy chapter. The project is implemented by the Cleaner Production Centre in Serbia (CPCS) at Belgrade University and in cooperation with the Ministry of Environmental Protection.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Mot bakgrund av en f&#xf6;rfr&#xe5;gan fr&#xe5;n det serbiska milj&#xf6;ministeriet inleddes andra fasen av ett projekt f&#xf6;r att minska industrins utsl&#xe4;pp och st&#xe4;rka Serbiens tilln&#xe4;rmning till EU och genomf&#xf6;randet av Integrated Pollution Prevention and Control (IPPC) samt Industrial Emissions Directive (IED) med ett s&#xe4;rskilt fokus p&#xe5; matindustrin. Projektet bidrar med underlag f&#xf6;r att f&#xf6;rbereda Serbiens f&#xf6;rhandlingsposition av Kapitel 27, EU:s milj&#xf6;lagstiftning. Projektet genomf&#xf6;rs av Cleaner Production Centre Serbia (CPCS) vid Belgrad Universitet och i samarbete med Milj&#xf6;ministeriet.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The general objective is to support the Serbian authorities and&#xa0;a selection of companies (operators) in the food production chain in the implementation of the EU&#xa0;Industrial Emission Directive (IED), in order to&#xa0;foster&#xa0;technological improvement and reduce the&#xa0;impact on&#xa0;the environment (i.e air, water, energy efficiency).
Specific components are:
1) Supporting the preparation of Negotiation Position for Chapter 27.&#xa0; Sweden and Serbia cooperate on EU environmental&#xa0;reform in Serbia, the environmental&#xa0;and climate Chapter 27. Under the first component support prepared the legislative framework in Serbia implementing the EU Industrial Emission Directive (IED).
2) Technical support to companies and competent authorities involved in the process of issuance and control of integrated permits for installations in the food sector.
3) Promotion of technological improvement in the food production chain. Promoting economic integration with the EU and development of market economy and develop innovative market opportunities.
4) Awareness and capacity building through education and events.
The project is implemented by the Cleaner Production Center at the Faculty of Technology and Metallurgy (Belgrade University), in cooperation with the Serbian Ministry of Environmental Protection.</narrative>
  </description>
